{"user_id": "ad7dba26-38fb-4b54-9155-059580fef06c", "user_name": "Vaishnavi D", "timestamp": "2026-09-02T17:04:37.399249+00:00", "question": "What is operational technology (OT) according to the NIST definition described by GAO?", "mode": "fixed_5", "answer": "According to the NIST definition described by GAO, operational technology (OT) is a broader designation that encompasses industrial control systems. Specifically, NIST guidance states that industrial control systems are an example of OT. The NIST Guide to Operational Technology (OT) Security, SP 800-82, Rev. 3, expands the scope of its guidance on industrial control systems security to include OT security and characterizes industrial control systems as part of operational technology. Therefore, operational technology (OT) includes systems such as supervisory control and data acquisition systems, distributed control systems, and building automation systems.", "sources": [{"document": "d24106576.pdf", "page": 45, "rank": 1, "distance": 0.7399188280105591}, {"document": "d24106576.pdf", "page": 9, "rank": 2, "distance": 0.7605215907096863}, {"document": "d24106576.pdf", "page": 13, "rank": 3, "distance": 0.843988835811615}, {"document": "d24106576.pdf", "page": 14, "rank": 4, "distance": 0.9044535160064697}, {"document": "d24106576.pdf", "page": 45, "rank": 5, "distance": 0.9763673543930054}], "telemetry": {"query": "What is operational technology (OT) according to the NIST definition described by GAO?", "query_intent": "definition", "query_complexity": "medium", "query_word_count": 13, "query_entity_count": 3, "is_multi_hop": true, "requires_multiple_sources": true, "initial_k": 5, "predicted_k": 5, "predicted_k_confidence": null, "predicted_k_probabilities": null, "selected_k": 5, "maximum_k": 5, "retrieval_iterations": 1, "retrieval_strategy": "fixed_baseline", "num_retrieved_chunks": 5, "num_chunks_used": 5, "unique_documents": 1, "retrieval_time_ms": 222.40269999019802, "generation_time_ms": 90634.0699999127