{"user_id": "ad7dba26-38fb-4b54-9155-059580fef06c", "user_name": "Vaishnavi D", "timestamp": "2026-09-02T17:07:04.139303+00:00", "question": "What is operational technology (OT) according to the NIST definition described by GAO?", "mode": "fixed_10", "answer": "According to the NIST definition described by GAO, operational technology (OT) is described as \"a broad range of programmable systems and devices that interact with the physical environment (or manage devices that interact with the physical environment).\" These systems and devices detect or cause a direct change through monitoring and/or control of devices, processes, and events. Additionally, examples of OT include supervisory control and data acquisition systems, distributed control systems, and building automation systems.", "sources": [{"document": "d24106576.pdf", "page": 45, "rank": 1, "distance": 0.7399188280105591}, {"document": "d24106576.pdf", "page": 9, "rank": 2, "distance": 0.7605215907096863}, {"document": "d24106576.pdf", "page": 13, "rank": 3, "distance": 0.843988835811615}, {"document": "d24106576.pdf", "page": 14, "rank": 4, "distance": 0.9044535160064697}, {"document": "d24106576.pdf", "page": 45, "rank": 5, "distance": 0.9763673543930054}, {"document": "d24106576.pdf", "page": 12, "rank": 6, "distance": 0.9864591360092163}, {"document": "d24106576.pdf", "page": 26, "rank": 7, "distance": 1.0307010412216187}, {"document": "d24106576.pdf", "page": 2, "rank": 8, "distance": 1.0395342111587524}, {"document": "d24106576.pdf", "page": 7, "rank": 9, "distance": 1.1251769065856934}, {"document": "d24105658.pdf", "page": 72, "rank": 10, "distance": 1.1314597129821777}], "telemetry": {"query": "What is operational technology (OT) according to the NIST definition described by GAO?", "query_intent": "definition", "query_complexity": "medium", "query_word_count": 13, "query_entity_count": 3, "is_multi_hop": true, "requires_multiple_sources": true, "initial_k": 10, "predicted_k": 10, "predicted_k_conf