{"user_id": "ad7dba26-38fb-4b54-9155-059580fef06c", "user_name": "Vaishnavi D", "timestamp": "2026-09-03T04:27:42.891708+00:00", "question": "What information-security responsibilities does the head of a federal agency have under the FISMA framework described by GAO?", "mode": "fixed_3", "answer": "Under the FISMA framework described by GAO, the head of a federal agency has the responsibility to develop, document, and implement an agency-wide information security program. This program must include procedures for detecting, reporting, and responding to security incidents. Additionally, the head of the agency is required to report annually on the total number of information security incidents to the Office of Management and Budget (OMB) and Congress. The head of the agency must also ensure compliance with OMB’s policies and procedures, the Department of Homeland Security’s binding operational directives, and the National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST) federal information standards and guidelines.", "sources": [{"document": "d24105658.pdf", "page": 12, "rank": 1, "distance": 0.7394595742225647}, {"document": "d24105658.pdf", "page": 2, "rank": 2, "distance": 0.8130574226379395}, {"document": "d24105658.pdf", "page": 28, "rank": 3, "distance": 0.840805172920227}], "telemetry": {"query": "What information-security responsibilities does the head of a federal agency have under the FISMA framework described by GAO?", "query_intent": "general", "query_complexity": "medium", "query_word_count": 19, "query_entity_count": 3, "is_multi_hop": false, "requires_multiple_sources": true, "initial_k": 3, "predicted_k": 3, "predicted_k_confidence": null, "predicted_k_probabilities": null, "selected_k": 3, "maximum_k": 3, "retrieval_iterations": 1, "retrieval_strategy": "fixed_baseline", "num_retrieved_chunks": 3, "num_chunks_used": 3, "unique_documents": 1, "retrieval_time_ms": 324.21350001823157, "generation_time_ms": 108050.17119995318, "optimization_time_ms": 0.4430999